# Component reuse

Figma build order: design system → atoms → sections → pages.

Before creating a component, check `src/registry/components.json` and `src/components/`.

## Atoms (`src/components/ui/`)

Restyle the existing primitive to match Figma (Button, Headline, Form, InfoCard, ServiceCard, IconPoint). Do not add a second button or a page-specific heading component.

## Sections (`src/components/widgets/`)

One pattern = one widget for the whole site:

- FAQ accordion → `FAQs` (every page that has FAQs)
- Hero → `Hero2`
- Page CTA band → `CTABanner`
- Quotes → `Testimonials`
- Split + image → `Content`

If Figma’s FAQ (or hero, CTA, …) looks different, restyle **that** widget. Pass copy and `isDark` as props. Do not create `HomeFAQ.astro` / `ServicesFAQ.astro`.

## New UI

New unique Figma shape → **one** new component, then add it to `src/registry/components.json` (`id`, `figmaNames`, `shape`, `component`, `import`). Never paste one-off markup into a page file.

Do not pick layouts from item counts (band vs grid vs cards). Figma already decided.

Cards with a link or button: card `flex flex-col h-full`, body `flex-1`, CTA `mt-auto` so links line up regardless of copy length.
